mac_do_auto is a FreeBSD MAC policy kernel module that transparently
grants privileges to processes whose credentials include membership in a
configured group (default: wheel/GID 0), without requiring explicit use
of mdo(1), sudo(8), or doas(1).

Features:
  * mac_priv_grant hook with per-jail enable/disable/inherit policy
  * Privilege scoping by category (system, vfs, net, jail, ...) via
    sysctl security.mac.autodo.scope
  * /dev/autodo character device with a ring buffer of audit events
    (poll/kqueue/ioctl interface)
  * autodo-eventd companion daemon: UCL configuration, multi-group
    policy with templates, JSON audit log

The module is configured via the security.mac.autodo.* sysctl tree and
the daemon via /usr/local/etc/autodo/autodo.conf.
